# GalaxyXR-Driver

Read `AGENTS.md` first. Source roots are `GalaxyXRDriver/` (C++17) and
`GalaxyXRDriverGUI/` (TypeScript/Lit + Tauri). `CustomHeadsetOpenVR` is the
neutral runtime identity; `GalaxyXRNative` is the Galaxy XR build.

## Build and test

- Package: `node build.js --vendor galaxyxr` (or `--vendor neutral`).
- Portable build (required at end of plan): `tools/Build-Portable.ps1`.
- Focused checks: `tools/Test-*.ps1` and `tools/Test-*.cjs`.
- Rust backend: `cargo test --locked --lib` in `GalaxyXRDriverGUI/src-tauri`.
- Generated output belongs under `../builds/GalaxyXR-Driver/`; never create
  `build/`, `dist/`, `target/` or caches inside the checkout.
- Every completed plan runs the full local portable build before reporting complete.

## Rules

- Preserve setting schemas, migrations, defaults and the driver/Companion
  contract. Reject invalid values visibly; do not silently clamp them.
- Preserve installer backup, rollback, ownership-journal and refusal behavior.
- Never rewrite `ThirdParty/`, vendor binaries or supplied artifacts in place.
- Keep PowerShell 5.1 compatibility in `.ps1` files used by `.cmd` launchers.
- Do not deploy drivers, mutate SteamVR or touch a headset without explicit
  authorization.
- State separately what was statically checked, compiled, CI-verified or proven
  on hardware.

